From e172350667b40b44bf08ed28b0faba1eb163ed47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:47:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: uvcvideo: no autosuspend for the T1 iBridge in
 configuration 2

The T1 iBridge is a composite device: camera, Touch Bar display and
digitizer, private network link and Secure Enclave transport. In USB
configuration 2 (as macOS uses it) enabling autosuspend from the UVC probe
changes power policy for all of them. Configuration 1 (camera, Touch Bar
keys, ambient light) keeps the upstream behaviour.

Same intent as t1bridge's 0002 (Andrew Boyd), which sets the quirk for the
device in every configuration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: Linux drivers/media/usb/uvc (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git)
---
 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c
index 22b1c30..0496d13 100644
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c
@@ -2441,6 +2441,17 @@ static int uvc_probe(struct usb_interface *intf,
 	if (dev->quirks & UVC_QUIRK_NO_RESET_RESUME)
 		udev->quirks &= ~USB_QUIRK_RESET_RESUME;
 
+	/*
+	 * The Apple T1 iBridge (05ac:8600) is one USB device for the camera,
+	 * Touch Bar, network link and Secure Enclave. In configuration 2 (the
+	 * one macOS uses) autosuspend from this probe would suspend the other
+	 * functions too; configuration 1 keeps the usual behaviour.
+	 */
+	if (le16_to_cpu(udev->descriptor.idVendor) == 0x05ac &&
+	    le16_to_cpu(udev->descriptor.idProduct) == 0x8600 &&
+	    udev->actconfig && udev->actconfig->desc.bConfigurationValue == 2)
+		dev->quirks |= UVC_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND;
+
 	if (!(dev->quirks & UVC_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND))
 		usb_enable_autosuspend(udev);
 
-- 
